283
00:10:08,676 --> 00:10:09,474
them.

284
00:10:09,717 --> 00:10:12,303
The New York Fed also measures the

285
00:10:12,303 --> 00:10:13,937
stock of bad debt.

286
00:10:14,097 --> 00:10:16,136
The share of card balances that were

287
00:10:16,136 --> 00:10:18,401
ninety days or more behind rose from

288
00:10:18,401 --> 00:10:20,666
seven point six percent in late twenty

289
00:10:20,666 --> 00:10:22,705
twenty-two to twelve point eight percent

290
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:25,117
in early twenty twenty-six.

291
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,046
And more than twenty-three million

292
00:10:27,046 --> 00:10:29,575
Americans still carry card debts on their

293
00:10:29,575 --> 00:10:32,103
credit reports that lenders have already

294
00:10:32,103 --> 00:10:33,393
written off.

295
00:10:33,650 --> 00:10:35,967
Let me put the three businesses side

296
00:10:35,967 --> 00:10:37,030
by side.

297
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,793
The toll on every swipe,

298
00:10:38,793 --> 00:10:41,460
collected by the networks and the banks.

299
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:42,904
The interest,

300
00:10:42,904 --> 00:10:46,070
paid by people who carry a balance.

301
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:46,590
And the fees,

302
00:10:46,590 --> 00:10:47,990
paid by people who slip.

303
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,823
Three streams of money,

304
00:10:49,823 --> 00:10:52,787
all flowing through the same small card.

305
00:10:53,050 --> 00:10:55,793
So what is the hidden business behind

306
00:10:55,793 --> 00:10:57,390
your credit card?

307
00:10:57,790 --> 00:10:59,720
It is not the plastic.

308
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:01,450
It is the position.

309
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:04,280
The card sits between you and every

310
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:04,766
store,

311
00:11:04,766 --> 00:11:07,838
and every company in that chain takes

312
00:11:07,838 --> 00:11:08,950
a slice.

313
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:10,366
If you pay in full,

314
00:11:10,366 --> 00:11:12,790
the system can work in your favor.

315
00:11:12,950 --> 00:11:14,562
If you carry a balance,

316
00:11:14,562 --> 00:11:16,590
you are the one paying for it.

317
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:17,558
Either way,

318
00:11:17,558 --> 00:11:20,124
the card is never really free.

319
00:11:20,384 --> 00:11:22,981
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

320
00:11:22,981 --> 00:11:26,078
we follow the money behind another hidden

321
00:11:26,078 --> 00:11:28,584
link of the world economy.

322
00:11:28,594 --> 00:11:30,837
This is The Hidden Economics.
